  "label": "User projected onto the distorted image of the white woman",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the distorted white woman (woman_in_top_panel) in the top panel of the meme. This projection is implicit, as the meme uses the exaggerated image and the label 'average white \"women\"' to represent a generalized, stereotypical 'average white woman' that the user is expected to identify with or see as a representation of themselves or their group. The distortion and labeling create a visual and textual anchor for the user to project their own identity or perception onto, reinforcing the harmful stereotype that white women are 'hysterical' or 'overreactive'.",
